Snapshot of the standard library (enzarb/workflows, commit 2b5ae0d) for engine tests that
route and run real workflow definitions. Refresh by copying the library files again.

Differences from that commit (issue #273): the workflow-level `commands:` defaults
(workflows/issue.yaml, workflows/pull_request.yaml), the `retry` override of the `checks` wait
(phases/review_rounds.yaml), the `feedback_since` watermark of `address_human` and
the `not event.command` guard of the triage answer waits and prompts/address.md rendering `pr.feedback`. The library repo gets the same change as its own PR;
until then this snapshot is ahead of it.

Environment failures (issue #300, ADR-0026): every agent step lists `platform_wait` for
`disk_full` and `oom`, so such a failure waits (`reason: platform_wait`) and resumes the same
run instead of following the phase's edges (`review/rounds/human`, a fix round,
`implement/blocked`). `network` and `load` are not listed (`sandbox.healthy` is too coarse an
`until`: docs/gaps.md #22); with `toolchain_missing` and `unknown` they follow the edges, as does
any failure with no `environment`. `checks`, `prepare` and `context` never wait. `tests/library.rs`
(`library_environment_*`, `library_code_failure_*`) covers the routing. The upstream
`enzarb/workflows` v1.6.0 carries the same `platform_wait` lists.
